==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Pirate Cat's knockback chance from 10% to 30%.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Pirate Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Shonen Manga (Removed Combo)|Shonen Manga]] and [[Patched Up (Removed Combo)|Patched Up]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Pirate Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Pirate Cat
Influenced by a certain pirate cartoon,
and dreams of being a Pirate King. Can't swim.
Might knockback Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Captain Cat
Still thinks Pirates are cool. Still can't swim.
Doesn't get along with Ninja Cat anymore.
Might knockback Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Dread Pirate Catley
Just learned that there are movies about
pirates too! Inspired him to upgrade his boat.
Might knockback Red enemies.</pre>
**Captain Cat's original description used to reference the rivalry that was once prominent between ''One Piece'' and another popular manga/anime series, ''[[wikipedia:Naruto|Naruto]]'', as Naruto is about ninjas and Captain Cat "doesn't get along with [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] anymore".
*Pirate Cat's description references the popular manga/anime series ''[[wikipedia:One Piece|One Piece]].'' In the series, the protagonist expresses his wish of becoming the King of the Pirates basically every time he has a chance to.
**Captain Cat's description also references One Piece's devil fruit and their side effect of making you unable to swim.
*Dread Pirate Catley's English name references a character from ''[[wikipedia:The Princess Bride|The Princess Bride]]'': [[wikipedia:Dread Pirate Roberts|Dread Pirate Roberts]], whose real name, Westley, can be combined with "Cat" to form "Catley".
*Dread Pirate Catley's Japanese name, Nyack Sparrow (ニャック・スパロウ ''Nyakku Suparō''), is a reference to the ''Pirates of the Caribbean'' character [[wikia:pirates:Jack Sparrow|Jack Sparrow]].

